          <span class="card-cta">Traeger repair details →</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="hub-section hub-section-gray">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>How our techs approach outdoor smokers</h2>
      <p>Two architectures dominate: ceramic kamados (Big Green Egg, Kamado Joe, Primo) — primary service items are gasket replacement (year 3-5 typical, $145-$245), dome thermometer accuracy (calibration check, $85-$145 if replacement needed), and hardware service (hinges, bands, dampers). Ceramic damage is warranty-navigated; Big Green Egg specifically has a lifetime ceramic warranty we help customers access. Pellet smokers (Traeger, Memphis) — service items include auger motor service (the pellet-feed mechanism), igniter replacement (year 2-4 typical), controller diagnostics, and WiFi-connectivity troubleshooting on the modern WiFIRE units.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="hub-section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Is the Big Green Egg lifetime ceramic warranty legitimate?</summary>
          <p>Yes, but the navigation matters. The warranty covers ceramic body cracking under normal use to original purchaser. We document failure on-site and coordinate with the customer through BGE's warranty process — they ship the replacement ceramic component, we install. Labor is separately billable. This is the most genuinely warranted product in the smoker category.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>My Traeger pellet auger is jamming. What's wrong?</summary>
          <p>Almost always pellet quality or moisture absorption — Traeger pellets that have absorbed humidity swell and jam the auger feed. Less commonly: auger motor wear (year 3-5 typical), or controller-board issue interrupting feed signals. We diagnose by removing pellets, inspecting the auger directly, and testing motor function.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Should I winterize my smoker for LA winters?</summary>
          <p>Not strictly necessary — LA winters don't typically threaten ceramic kamados or weather-protected pellet smokers. We do recommend covering the unit when not in use (UV degrades gaskets and seals over time) and bringing pellet smokers indoors during heavy-rain weeks if they're not under permanent shelter.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
